Based on the context provided, when a streaming resume attempt fails with HTTP 409 (checkpoint mismatch), the server's error payload includes a structured error message with the following JSON schema:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "error": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "code": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 409
        },
        "message": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "data": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "truncation_preview": {
              "type": "object"
            },
            "resume_details": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "prefix_hash": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "resume_token": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "resume_offset": {
                  "type": "integer"
                },
                "resume_reason": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The `kv_crc` value inside v2 resume tokens is computed by taking the cyclic redundancy check (CRC) of the key-value pair in the resume token, and then taking the CRC of that CRC value. This process is repeated a number of times (typically 3 or more) to ensure that the resulting CRC value is robust against errors and collisions
